-- title:
--   Normality of a flat base change from reduced special fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $R$, $B$, $R'$, $K'$, $k'$ be commutative rings in a common universe, with $B$ an $R$-algebra that is flat as an $R$-module, and $R'$ an $R$-algebra. Let $\varpi \in R'$ be a non-zero-divisor. Let $K'$ be an $R'$-algebra realising the localisation of $R'$ away from $\varpi$, and also an $R$-algebra, compatibly (the tower $R \to R' \to K'$ commutes), and assume that $K' \otimes_R B$ is a domain and is integrally closed (in its fraction field). Let $k'$ be an $R'$-algebra and an $R$-algebra, again compatibly, and assume that the structure map $R' \to k'$ is surjective with kernel the ideal generated by $\varpi$, and that $k' \otimes_R B$ is reduced. Then $R' \otimes_R B$ is a domain and is integrally closed. The conclusion is stated as the conjunction of the two assertions.
--
--   This is the standard criterion, in the form used for affine charts of arithmetic models, that a flat base change with integrally closed domain generic fibre and reduced special fibre is itself an integrally closed domain; the proof goes through the statements that $R' \otimes_R B$ is integrally closed in its localisation away from $\varpi \otimes 1$ (via reducedness of the quotient by $\varpi$) and that this localisation is $K' \otimes_R B$. It is used to establish normality of chart rings of integral models of modular curves of full level after base change, in particular in the analysis of their fibres over ramified discrete valuation rings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_TensorProduct_isDomain_and_isIntegrallyClosed_of_isReduced_fibre.lean

